## Coding Standards

### General
- **Functional components only** — never class components
- **async/await** with try/catch — never `.then/.catch` promise chains
- **axios** for all API calls — import from `axios`
- Check existing components before creating new ones — **no duplicates**
- No TypeScript — plain `.jsx` files only
- No CSS Modules — styling via Tailwind utilities only

### Tailwind & Styling
- Every hardcoded light color must have a `dark:` variant counterpart
- Light card backgrounds: `bg-white` → add `dark:bg-[#1e293b]`
- Light page background: `dark:bg-[#0f172a]`
- Elevated card inside dark panel: `dark:bg-[#263446]`
- Primary text: `dark:text-slate-100`, secondary: `dark:text-slate-400`
- Colored stat/badge pattern (vivid glow): `dark:bg-[color]-500/25 dark:text-[color]-200 dark:border dark:border-[color]-500/50`
- Borders: `dark:border-slate-700`
- Do **not** add a `tailwind.config.js` — Tailwind v4 config is in `index.css` under `@theme`

### Custom Dropdown Pattern (`FilterDropdown`)
- **Never use native `<select>`** for custom-styled dropdowns — create a controlled React component instead
- `FilterDropdown` is the established pattern:
  - Trigger button shows current value + `ChevronDown` icon; rotates icon on open
  - Trigger turns orange-tinted (`bg-orange-50 border-orange-300`) when a non-default option is selected
  - Panel: `absolute`, `mt-2` gap from trigger, `rounded-2xl`, `shadow-lg`, `z-50`, `min-w-[160px]`
  - Selected option: orange background + bold text + `Check` icon on the right
  - Close on outside click via `useRef` + `useEffect` (`mousedown` event on `document`)
  - Active filter count badge shown on the SlidersHorizontal trigger button

### MUI Icons & Components
- Import icons from `@mui/icons-material`, not `@mui/material`
- Brand orange `#d97757` icons are fine in both light and dark modes
- Navy `#1d3557` icon colors must use `useTheme()` to conditionally become `#e2e8f0` in dark mode:
  ```jsx
  const { isDark } = useTheme();
  <Icon sx={{ color: isDark ? "#e2e8f0" : "#1d3557" }} />
  ```
- MUI Paper/Dialog/Menu backgrounds must be set via `sx` using `isDark` for dark mode

### Dark Mode
- `ThemeContext` at `src/frontend/context/ThemeContext.jsx` owns dark mode state
- `useTheme()` hook exposes `{ isDark, toggleTheme }`
- The `dark` class is toggled on `document.documentElement` (`<html>`)
- Custom Tailwind variant: `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *))` in `index.css`
- Chart.js colors (axes, legend) must be computed dynamically using `isDark` from `useTheme()`

